course: dictionary
lesson: 6919
title: Pacific: an ocean and a word for peace
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a capital letter because they are names, and some do not. Pacific can be a name or an ordinary word. «The Pacific Ocean is the largest and the deepest ocean.» Here Pacific is a name, so it means a huge ocean, not a feeling.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «He found an ocean so calm that he named it the Pacific, meaning peaceful.» The sentence tells you that Pacific means peaceful, and the word calm is another clue that it is about peace.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you read «a pacific mood» and it means a peaceful mood, your meaning fits. Pacific is a formal word, so you will meet it more in books and speeches than in everyday talk.
fact: The Pacific Ocean is the largest and deepest ocean on Earth.
fact: The Pacific lies between Asia and Australia on one side and the Americas on the other.
fact: The Pacific covers about a third of the Earth's surface and has thousands of islands, such as Hawaii, Fiji and New Zealand.
fact: The Mariana Trench, the deepest place in the oceans, is in the Pacific.
fact: «Pacific» as an adjective is formal and means peaceful or wanting peace.
exercise: «The Pacific Ocean is the largest and the deepest ocean.» What is the Pacific here? | A small lake in the hills | A kind of canoe | A type of storm | *A huge ocean on Earth
exercise: Which of these is one of the five oceans in «There are five oceans: the Pacific, the Atlantic, the Indian, the Southern and the Arctic»? | *Atlantic | Cyclone | Typhoon | Hurricane
exercise: Ella says a pacific mood is a wild, noisy one. What does pacific mean? | *Peaceful, wanting peace | Wild and noisy | Fast and rushing | Very cold
test: Where is the Pacific Ocean, roughly? | In the middle of the Sahara | Under the Arctic ice | Between Africa and Europe | *Between Asia and Australia on one side and the Americas on the other
test: The Pacific has a famous "Ring of Fire" with many volcanoes and earthquakes. Which storm is called a typhoon in the north-west Pacific? | *The storm near the Philippines and Japan | The storm in the Atlantic | The storm on a mountain lake | The storm in the Sahara
exam: Which sentence uses pacific to mean peaceful? | «The Pacific Ocean is the largest ocean.» | *«After the argument, both leaders wanted a pacific end to the fight.» | «Polynesian navigators crossed the Pacific in double canoes.» | «Hawaii and Fiji are Pacific Islands.»
